                haunted hotel, a theater night, a lock-in. Events aren't part of any plan. Each one is
                bought on its own, by a group or by the person organizing it.
            </p>

            <div class="row g-4">
                <div class="col-12 col-lg-7">
                    <article class="plan-inclusions__card h-100">
                        <h3 class="h5 mb-3">What an event includes</h3>
                        <ul class="plan-inclusions__list" data-testid="pricing-event-features">
                            <li><BenIcon Name="check-circle" /><span>A plan of the rooms or seats, drawn once and reused the next time you're at that venue</span></li>
                            <li><BenIcon Name="check-circle" /><span>Bookings: guests pick a room or seat or ask for one, with places held while you decide, and a booking board to confirm, move or turn people down</span></li>
                            <li><BenIcon Name="check-circle" /><span>A program of sessions that guests sign up for</span></li>
                            <li><BenIcon Name="check-circle" /><span>Menus for each night, dining tables with who sits where, and a dietary sheet for the kitchen</span></li>
                            <li><BenIcon Name="check-circle" /><span>A QR pass for every party, checked in at the door from a phone, and wristband colors</span></li>
                            <li><BenIcon Name="check-circle" /><span>Staff with only the rights they need: the door, the guest list, bookings, the kitchen or files</span></li>
                            <li><BenIcon Name="check-circle" /><span>The event's own public page and gallery, files for guests, and a room where guests talk and share photos</span></li>
                            <li><BenIcon Name="check-circle" /><span>Letters to your guests, then a thank-you, reviews and a list of who came</span></li>
                            <li><BenIcon Name="check-circle" /><span>@StorageWords(offer.StorageMegabytes) for each event's files and photos, kept for @offer.FilesKeptDays days after it ends, with a download to keep them</span></li>
                            <li><BenIcon Name="check-circle" /><span>Guests book for free. The site never takes their money; you settle payment with them yourselves.</span></li>
                        </ul>
                    </article>
                </div>

                <div class="col-12 col-lg-5">
                    <article class="plan-inclusions__card pricing-events__buy h-100" data-testid="pricing-event-offer">
                        <h3 class="h5 mb-2">One event, one credit</h3>
                        <div class="pricing-events__price">
                            <span class="pricing-band__amount" data-testid="pricing-event-price">@BenMoney.Format(offer.UnitPrice)</span>
                            <span class="pricing-band__per">per event</span>
                        </div>
                        <p class="small mb-1" data-testid="pricing-event-subscriber-price">
                            <strong>@BenMoney.Format(offer.SubscriberUnitPrice)</strong> for a group with a paid plan
                            (@offer.SubscriberPercent.ToString("0.##")% of the price).
                        </p>
                        <p class="small text-secondary mb-3">plus sales tax where your state requires it</p>

                        @if (bundles.Count > 0)
                        {
                            <ul class="plan-inclusions__list small mb-3" data-testid="pricing-event-bundles">
                                @foreach (var b in bundles)
                                {
                                    <li><BenIcon Name="package" /><span>@b.Quantity events for @BenMoney.Format(b.FullPrice) — @BenMoney.Format(b.SubscriberPrice) with a paid plan</span></li>
                                }
                            </ul>
                        }

                        <ul class="plan-inclusions__list small mb-3">
                            <li><BenIcon Name="check-circle" /><span>One credit covers one event, however many days in a row it runs.</span></li>
                            <li><BenIcon Name="check-circle" /><span>An event is paid for when you first publish it. Drafts are free.</span></li>
                            <li><BenIcon Name="check-circle" /><span>Each one is good for @offer.LifeDays days. The event's first date has to fall before it runs out.</span></li>
                            <li><BenIcon Name="check-circle" /><span>Call an event off at least @offer.CancellationWindowHours hours before it starts and you get it back to use again.</span></li>
                        </ul>

                        @if (!offer.OnSale)
                        {
                            <p class="alert alert-secondary mb-0 py-2">Events aren't on sale at the moment.</p>
                        }
                        else if (UserState.IsAuthenticated)
                        {
                            <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2 align-items-end">
                                <div class="flex-grow-1" style="min-width: 10rem;">
                                    <label class="form-label small mb-1" for="pricing-event-group">For</label>
                                    <select id="pricing-event-group" class="form-select" data-testid="pricing-event-group"
                                            @onchange="@(e => _eventBuyer = e.Value?.ToString() ?? "")">
                                        @if (_myGroups.Count != 1)
                                        {
                                            <option value="" selected="@(_eventBuyer == "")">Choose</option>
                                        }
                                        @foreach (var (org, _) in _myGroups)
                                        {
                                            <option value="@org.Id" selected="@(_eventBuyer == org.Id.ToString() || (_eventBuyer == "" && _myGroups.Count == 1))">@org.Name</option>
                                        }
                                        <option value="me" selected="@(_eventBuyer == "me")">Myself — credits I hold</option>
                                    </select>
                                </div>
                                @if (bundles.Count > 0)
                                {
                                    <div style="min-width: 9rem;">
                                        <label class="form-label small mb-1" for="pricing-event-bundle">Buy</label>
                                        <select id="pricing-event-bundle" class="form-select" data-testid="pricing-event-bundle"
                                                @onchange="@(e => _eventBundle = int.TryParse(e.Value?.ToString(), out var q) ? q : null)">
                                            <option value="" selected="@(_eventBundle is null)">Single events</option>
                                            @foreach (var b in bundles)
                                            {
                                                <option value="@b.Quantity" selected="@(_eventBundle == b.Quantity)">Bundle of @b.Quantity</option>
                                            }
                                        </select>
                                    </div>
                                }
                                @if (_eventBundle is null)
                                {
                                    <div style="width: 6.5rem;">
                                        <label class="form-label small mb-1" for="pricing-event-quantity">How many</label>
                                        <input id="pricing-event-quantity" type="number" class="form-control"
                                               min="1" max="@offer.MaximumPerPurchase" data-testid="pricing-event-quantity"
                                               @bind="_eventQuantity" @bind:event="oninput" />
                                    </div>
                                }
                                <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary text-nowrap" data-testid="pricing-buy-events"
                                        disabled="@(_buyingEvents || (_eventBundle is null && (_eventQuantity < 1 || _eventQuantity > offer.MaximumPerPurchase)))"
                                        @onclick="BuyEventsAsync">
                                    @(_buyingEvents ? "Opening…" : $"Buy {EventCountShown(offer)} for {BenMoney.Format(EventPriceShown(offer))}")
                                </button>
                            </div>
                            @if (_eventError is not null)
                            {
                                <div class="alert alert-danger mt-2 mb-0 py-2" role="alert">@_eventError</div>
                            }
                            <p class="small text-secondary mt-2 mb-0">
                                Credits you buy for yourself are on <a href="/my-event-credits">My event credits</a>.
                            </p>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <a class="btn btn-outline-primary" href="@Ben.Web.Website.Library.Kit.SignInLink.For("pricing#events")">Sign in to buy events</a>
                        }
                    </article>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    };

